### Store-binding root cause located (for the next session)

The durable runtime resolves its store in `resolveStoreResources`
(`plugin-sagas-core@0.0.7/src/runtime/saga-durable-runtime.ts`): `options.backend === 'prisma'` +
`options.prisma` client → `PrismaSagaStore`; otherwise the KV store. The runner composition
(`startSagaRunner`, `plugin-sagas/runtime`) reads only `SAGAS_ADAPTER` (native), the registry
module, and the projection — it never reads `NETSCRIPT_SAGA_STORE`, and our generated
`sagas/runtime.ts` passes only `{ registryModule }`. So the declared `Sagas.Store.Backend:
prisma` never reaches `resolveStoreResources`. Fix for the next session: in
`sagas/runtime.ts`, when `NETSCRIPT_SAGA_STORE === 'prisma'`, pass
`runtimeOptions.native.backend = 'prisma'` plus the workspace Prisma client
(`@ledgerline/db` — it has all five saga delegates the runtime type-guards for: sagaInstance,
sagaExecutionHistory, sagaRuntimeState, sagaRuntimeTransition, sagaRuntimeCorrelation), then
restart the sagas processor and re-drive; the instances API should then show terminal `failed`
for a chaos item. Everything else (effector undo, terminalise-from-.on, runtime tests) is
already in place.
EOF
